// A CHAIN OF MODULE GLOBALS read back through an expression that names two of them — the
// shape that made the COMPILER trap on a `vl check`-clean program (D1513). `globalCellKind`'s
// ~40-rung ladder re-enters itself through the `expr*` predicates, so each rung re-derived
// every referenced global from scratch: one added link MULTIPLIED the work instead of adding
// to it, and these seven lines exhausted the 4 GiB GC heap in ~9 s. Peak RSS 4.22 GB (trap)
// before, 47 MB after. Nothing here is exotic and none of it is about the empty literal — the
// annotated `P[]` spelling of the same chain trapped identically.
// Found 2026-09-03 by D1511's position matrix (#2480), `array_element` un-annotated; closed
// by the memo on that ladder. Kept as the probe that keeps it closed.
// Should print 3.
const xs0 = []
xs0.push({ y: 1, x: 2 })
const outer = [xs0]
const inner = outer[0]
const first = inner[0]
let acc = 0
print(first.y + inner[0].x + acc)
